export default function Page() {
  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: "<h1 id=\"the-self-evolving-harness\">The self-evolving harness</h1>\n<p>Most agent systems improve when <em>you</em> tune them. Athena tunes <strong>itself</strong> \u2014 and the\ndesign guarantees it cannot silently get worse.</p>\n<p>Every self-modification obeys three rules:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Gated</strong> \u2014 applied only when the evidence supports it.</li>\n<li><strong>Signed</strong> \u2014 written to the ledger as <code>EVOLVE_HARNESS</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Reversible</strong> \u2014 one command undoes it.</li>\n</ol>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena evolution        # what it has learned\nathena evolve           # run one pass (every operator, each independently gated)\nathena evolution revert # roll back the most recent change\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"what-it-learns-from\">What it learns from</h2>\n<p>Every finished task becomes an <strong>episode</strong>: the directive, the tier that ran it, whether\nit succeeded, and how many specialists worked it. Each dispatched specialist also records\nits own outcome (iterations used, whether it hit its cap, the failure signature).</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-operators\">The operators</h2>\n<h3 id=\"1-tier-routing\">1. Tier routing</h3>\n<p>Athena routes each directive to <code>fast</code>, <code>medium</code>, or <code>full</code>. From an outcome it infers\nthe tier that <em>should</em> have run \u2014 a fast/medium run that failed was under-powered; a full\nrun one specialist finished cleanly was over-powered. Mis-tiered directives become\nlearned exemplars for the router.</p>\n<p><strong>Gate:</strong> replay every recorded episode through the router with the candidate exemplars.\nCommit only on a net accuracy gain. (Measured 0% \u2192 100% on a mis-tiered set.)</p>\n<h3 id=\"2-iteration-budgets\">2. Iteration budgets</h3>\n<p>A specialist that keeps hitting its iteration cap <em>and</em> failing gets more room; one that\nalways finishes early gets less.</p>\n<p><strong>Gate:</strong> at least 4 dispatches, plus the cap-hit and failure rates.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-prompt-lessons\">3. Prompt lessons</h3>\n<p>When a role fails the same way repeatedly, the harness appends a lesson to its system\nprompt \u2014 \"you have repeatedly failed with X; handle it explicitly.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Gate:</strong> the same failure signature at least 3 times.</p>\n<h3 id=\"4-playbook-distillation\">4. Playbook distillation</h3>\n<p>A successful multi-specialist run is distilled into a reusable playbook (the directive\nplus the ordered roles that solved it), so similar work starts from a known-good plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Gate:</strong> success, at least 2 specialists, and no duplicate.</p>\n<h3 id=\"5-skill-promotion\">5. Skill promotion</h3>\n<p>A synthesized skill that has proven itself is <strong>pinned</strong> as a permanent, always-offered\ntool \u2014 so the swarm reuses it instead of re-synthesizing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Gate:</strong> promoted status, \u22655 uses, \u226580% success rate. Reverse with\n<code>athena evolution unpin &lt;id&gt;</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"6-specialist-retirement\">6. Specialist retirement</h3>\n<p>A specialist the router keeps dispatching to that almost always fails is retired from the\nroster. Never retires an unused or new specialist, and never drops the roster below a\nfloor. Reverse with <code>athena evolution unretire &lt;role&gt;</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"auto-evolve\">Auto-evolve</h2>\n<p>Off by default. Turn it on to run every operator automatically:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena evolution auto on --every 20   # after every 20 recorded episodes\n</code></pre>\n<p>Each change is still gated and signed, so an automatic pass carries the same guarantees\nas a manual one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"auditing-it\">Auditing it</h2>\n<p>Every accepted mutation appears in the ledger and in <code>athena evolution</code>, with the metric\nbefore and after. Because the ledger is hash-chained and signed, the record of how your\nagent changed itself is as tamper-evident as the work it did.</p>" }} />;
}
